1
00:01:42,650 --> 00:01:48,020
[When I Meet The Moon]

2
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:51,090
[Episode 20]

3
00:01:59,120 --> 00:01:59,560
You...

4
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:04,140
You're still awake?

5
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:09,610
I actually fell asleep.

6
00:02:10,690 --> 00:02:12,900
Is this movie that bad?

7
00:02:27,370 --> 00:02:28,430
When I'm with you,

8
00:02:29,870 --> 00:02:31,329
I fall asleep more easily.

9
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:33,860
Hmm.

10
00:02:45,750 --> 00:02:46,710
Fireworks.

11
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:48,590
Look, fireworks!

12
00:02:49,210 --> 00:02:51,180
Come on. Let's go watch the fireworks!

13
00:02:51,180 --> 00:02:52,380
Hurry, take me there.

14
00:02:53,060 --> 00:02:54,680
Hurry, let's go.

15
00:02:55,970 --> 00:02:56,590
Let's go.

16
00:03:07,190 --> 00:03:08,130
So beautiful.

17
00:03:09,320 --> 00:03:10,110
Yeah.

18
00:03:10,530 --> 00:03:11,420
It really is.

19
00:03:22,530 --> 00:03:23,440
Look at that one.

20
00:03:23,440 --> 00:03:24,440
So cool.

21
00:03:28,630 --> 00:03:29,430
Yeah.

22
00:03:29,780 --> 00:03:30,860
It really is cool.

23
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:50,240
There are a lot of people today.

24
00:03:53,790 --> 00:03:55,290
There really are.

25
00:03:57,430 --> 00:03:59,310
How do you usually

26
00:03:59,340 --> 00:04:00,130
celebrate the New Year?

27
00:04:00,130 --> 00:04:01,870
Do you watch the fireworks every year?

28
00:04:01,870 --> 00:04:03,680
When I was in college,
I spent New Year's with Xia.

29
00:04:03,680 --> 00:04:05,410
Sometimes, I spent it on my own.

30
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:08,860
But this is the first time
I've ever watched fireworks.

31
00:04:38,930 --> 00:04:39,740
From now on,

32
00:04:40,520 --> 00:04:42,380
let's spend New Year's together.

33
00:04:43,930 --> 00:04:44,740
Sure.

34
00:04:52,740 --> 00:04:53,600
Happy New Year.

35
00:04:56,100 --> 00:04:57,040
Happy New Year.

36
00:05:26,600 --> 00:05:27,970
Do you have any wishes

37
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:29,330
for the new year?

38
00:05:32,490 --> 00:05:33,290
Do you?

39
00:05:34,110 --> 00:05:35,409
I wish...

40
00:05:37,690 --> 00:05:39,070
I just wish

41
00:05:39,810 --> 00:05:42,070
for you to keep liking me a little longer.

42
00:05:44,570 --> 00:05:46,170
I'm sure that will come true.

43
00:05:50,040 --> 00:05:50,900
What about you?

44
00:05:52,480 --> 00:05:54,480
I hope everything goes well for you.

45
00:06:03,180 --> 00:06:04,180
Happy New Year.

46
00:06:05,430 --> 00:06:06,690
Another sneak attack?

47
00:06:07,500 --> 00:06:09,180
When else did I do a sneak attack?

48
00:06:09,180 --> 00:06:09,930
You did.

49
00:06:10,670 --> 00:06:12,070
That time you were drunk.

50
00:06:12,930 --> 00:06:13,390
When...

51
00:06:13,680 --> 00:06:14,740
When I was drunk...

52
00:06:16,270 --> 00:06:17,980
that doesn't count.

53
00:06:19,070 --> 00:06:21,600
Besides, who knows
who made the first move...

54
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:49,830
You're back.

55
00:06:52,180 --> 00:06:53,640
Your sister is still here.

56
00:06:54,680 --> 00:06:55,630
Where have you two been?

57
00:06:55,630 --> 00:06:56,960
Why are you back so late?

58
00:06:59,670 --> 00:07:00,740
Watching fireworks.

59
00:07:00,740 --> 00:07:02,270
We went to watch fireworks.

60
00:07:04,170 --> 00:07:05,030
Let me help you.

61
00:07:05,720 --> 00:07:07,620
I forgot it was New Year's Eve.

62
00:07:07,980 --> 00:07:08,630
Tangy,

63
00:07:08,660 --> 00:07:09,380
why didn't you ask me

64
00:07:09,380 --> 00:07:11,180
to spend New Year's Eve with you?

65
00:07:11,390 --> 00:07:12,930
I was too busy. I forgot.

66
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:14,730
Just put them there.

67
00:07:20,770 --> 00:07:21,830
Lili, you're back.

68
00:07:28,370 --> 00:07:29,970
What's going on with you two?

69
00:07:35,270 --> 00:07:36,270
Isn't it obvious?

70
00:07:38,630 --> 00:07:39,930
You guys are together?

71
00:07:49,500 --> 00:07:50,300
So are we.

72
00:08:12,180 --> 00:08:13,040
Tell me.

73
00:08:13,300 --> 00:08:14,570
What's going on?

74
00:08:16,740 --> 00:08:17,540
Well...

75
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:19,260
we met,

76
00:08:19,780 --> 00:08:21,430
and then...

77
00:08:23,440 --> 00:08:25,200
we just got together.

78
00:08:29,090 --> 00:08:29,890
Same here.

79
00:08:32,919 --> 00:08:33,980
Don't interrupt.

80
00:08:34,630 --> 00:08:35,600
One at a time.

81
00:08:35,929 --> 00:08:36,860
You two go first.

82
00:08:38,480 --> 00:08:39,940
When did you get together?

83
00:08:41,580 --> 00:08:43,340
We only got together today.

84
00:08:44,290 --> 00:08:45,790
You just got together today?

85
00:08:45,790 --> 00:08:46,790
It's true.

86
00:08:47,500 --> 00:08:48,700
We just got together.

87
00:08:49,240 --> 00:08:50,030
Tangy.

88
00:08:54,330 --> 00:08:55,560
You knew it all along.

89
00:08:57,300 --> 00:08:59,230
So I'm the only one who didn't know.

90
00:09:01,840 --> 00:09:02,600
You two have been

91
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:04,290
right under my nose this whole time.

92
00:09:04,290 --> 00:09:05,440
How did you two manage

93
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:07,500
to get together without me noticing?

94
00:09:07,670 --> 00:09:09,570
We're like dry tinder and a blazing fire.

95
00:09:09,570 --> 00:09:11,170
We couldn't help ourselves.

96
00:09:14,390 --> 00:09:15,000
Congsheng,

97
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:16,070
enough about us.

98
00:09:16,070 --> 00:09:17,000
Look over there.

99
00:09:17,100 --> 00:09:17,870
Look at them.

100
00:09:17,980 --> 00:09:19,780
They're already holding hands!

101
00:09:21,600 --> 00:09:22,660
What about you two?

102
00:09:22,700 --> 00:09:24,100
What's your situation?

103
00:09:26,340 --> 00:09:27,130
Lili.

104
00:09:27,240 --> 00:09:28,600
You're amazing.

105
00:09:28,630 --> 00:09:31,090
You even managed
to get Uncle to fall for you.

106
00:09:31,230 --> 00:09:33,460
Not really. It wasn't that hard.

107
00:09:34,730 --> 00:09:36,390
When did you two start dating?

108
00:09:37,480 --> 00:09:39,680
After that trip to the hot spring hotel.

109
00:09:41,980 --> 00:09:43,750
Did Lili make the first move?

110
00:09:44,050 --> 00:09:44,860
I courted her.

111
00:09:53,050 --> 00:09:55,910
All of a sudden,
there are two more couples around me.

112
00:09:55,910 --> 00:09:57,050
It seems like my guesthouse

113
00:09:57,050 --> 00:09:58,650
is a lucky place for romance.

114
00:10:03,250 --> 00:10:04,320
It's New Year's Eve, too.

115
00:10:04,320 --> 00:10:05,220
Two joys at once!

116
00:10:05,220 --> 00:10:06,550
Let's have a drink together.

117
00:10:06,550 --> 00:10:07,290
Sure.

118
00:10:07,290 --> 00:10:08,000
Cheers.

119
00:10:08,050 --> 00:10:08,790
Cheers.

120
00:10:08,790 --> 00:10:09,700
Happy New Year.

121
00:10:19,720 --> 00:10:20,920
I'll get going, Lili.

122
00:10:21,220 --> 00:10:22,010
I'll be there in a moment.

123
00:10:22,010 --> 00:10:22,440
Okay.

124
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:49,730
What are you eating?

125
00:10:51,120 --> 00:10:52,200
You scared me.

126
00:10:52,500 --> 00:10:53,460
Why are you here?

127
00:10:54,860 --> 00:10:55,650
So,

128
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:58,060
what are you treating me to for lunch?

129
00:10:58,400 --> 00:11:00,550
The company's packed lunch.

130
00:11:03,100 --> 00:11:04,530
Then dinner's on me tonight.

131
00:11:04,530 --> 00:11:05,590
What are we eating?

132
00:11:05,750 --> 00:11:08,150
That restaurant
we missed out on last time.

133
00:11:10,010 --> 00:11:10,670
Yun Li.

134
00:11:12,750 --> 00:11:13,550
Engineer Fu?

135
00:11:13,860 --> 00:11:14,820
You're here too.

136
00:11:16,700 --> 00:11:17,980
I'll come back later, then.

137
00:11:17,980 --> 00:11:19,300
I'm just about to leave.

138
00:11:19,300 --> 00:11:20,760
I'll leave you two to talk.

139
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:29,750
Yun Li.

140
00:11:30,340 --> 00:11:32,070
Was that Engineer Fu being shy?

141
00:11:34,010 --> 00:11:34,820
Was he?

142
00:11:37,390 --> 00:11:38,050
Jiameng.

143
00:11:38,050 --> 00:11:39,150
which restaurant did Engineer Fu

144
00:11:39,150 --> 00:11:41,010
ask you to book?

145
00:11:41,150 --> 00:11:41,860
Let me tell you,

146
00:11:41,860 --> 00:11:43,310
the food there is really expensive!

147
00:11:43,310 --> 00:11:44,500
You have to book a table

148
00:11:44,500 --> 00:11:45,550
a week in advance.

149
00:11:46,550 --> 00:11:47,880
Didn't you go last time?

150
00:11:49,720 --> 00:11:51,250
He's taking me there today.

151
00:11:51,860 --> 00:11:52,650
Yun Li,

152
00:11:52,670 --> 00:11:54,930
you have to seize the opportunity.

153
00:12:08,390 --> 00:12:09,830
I recommend this one for winter.

154
00:12:09,830 --> 00:12:11,150
It has notes of chestnut
and cashmere wood,

155
00:12:11,150 --> 00:12:12,950
which gives it a warm, cozy feel.

156
00:12:13,650 --> 00:12:15,850
This one with iris notes is also lovely.

157
00:12:15,960 --> 00:12:18,600
I'm looking for something
for my boyfriend.

158
00:12:20,340 --> 00:12:22,410
This one with leather and woody notes
is a good choice.

159
00:12:22,410 --> 00:12:23,240
Really?

160
00:12:25,370 --> 00:12:27,720
Do you have anything that might help

161
00:12:27,720 --> 00:12:29,290
people relax and sleep better?

162
00:12:29,290 --> 00:12:30,820
Then I'd recommend this one with vetiver.

163
00:12:30,820 --> 00:12:32,610
It has notes of lemon and lemongrass,

164
00:12:32,610 --> 00:12:34,540
and it's a good choice for men, too.

165
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:37,330
I... I'll take this one!

166
00:12:37,700 --> 00:12:38,460
Of course. Just a moment.

167
00:12:38,460 --> 00:12:39,720
I'll wrap it up for you.

168
00:12:42,290 --> 00:12:43,600
Focus on your work today.

169
00:12:43,600 --> 00:12:44,390
Don't wait for me.

170
00:12:44,390 --> 00:12:46,050
I'll go there by myself later.

171
00:12:46,460 --> 00:12:47,890
You're heading over this early?

172
00:12:47,890 --> 00:12:49,550
I'm shopping at Haitian Mall.

173
00:12:50,050 --> 00:12:51,290
Buying a gift for me?

174
00:12:52,050 --> 00:12:52,910
No.

175
00:12:54,890 --> 00:12:56,290
You always figure me out.

176
00:12:56,290 --> 00:12:58,020
You always spoil the surprise.

177
00:13:00,150 --> 00:13:01,460
Then I'll come over now.

178
00:13:01,460 --> 00:13:01,980
Okay.

179
00:13:05,080 --> 00:13:06,010
Catch the thief!

180
00:13:36,650 --> 00:13:37,320
Hello?

181
00:13:37,720 --> 00:13:38,320
Lili.

182
00:13:39,410 --> 00:13:40,170
I'm almost there.

183
00:13:40,170 --> 00:13:41,050
Where are you?

184
00:13:41,550 --> 00:13:42,460
I'm at...

185
00:13:42,870 --> 00:13:44,220
the bus stop

186
00:13:44,220 --> 00:13:45,460
across from Haitian Mall.

187
00:13:45,460 --> 00:13:46,000
Okay.

188
00:13:46,650 --> 00:13:47,620
Fu Shize,

189
00:13:48,270 --> 00:13:49,150
could you go to the restaurant

190
00:13:49,150 --> 00:13:50,960
and wait for me there?

191
00:13:51,050 --> 00:13:51,860
What's wrong?

192
00:13:54,980 --> 00:13:57,120
Lili, what happened?

193
00:13:57,250 --> 00:13:58,410
Nothing. Just...

194
00:13:58,700 --> 00:14:00,630
I had a bit of an incident.

195
00:14:02,750 --> 00:14:03,550
Lili.

196
00:14:04,070 --> 00:14:05,070
Wait for me there.

197
00:14:05,250 --> 00:14:06,380
I'll be right there.

198
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:42,530
What happened to your hand?

199
00:14:47,050 --> 00:14:48,710
The gift I bought for you

200
00:14:49,010 --> 00:14:50,370
got broken when I fell.

201
00:14:51,980 --> 00:14:52,770
I'm fine.

202
00:14:53,130 --> 00:14:54,170
I just fell.

203
00:14:54,730 --> 00:14:56,090
It's just a scrape.

204
00:14:56,120 --> 00:14:57,400
Are you hurt anywhere else?

205
00:14:57,400 --> 00:14:58,930
No, nowhere else.

206
00:14:59,130 --> 00:15:01,790
I'll just put some ointment
on it when I get home.

207
00:15:01,890 --> 00:15:02,480
Let's go.

208
00:15:04,130 --> 00:15:05,250
Come on, get in.

209
00:15:35,850 --> 00:15:38,850
[Steal A Moment To Sip Wine Guesthouse]

210
00:15:41,840 --> 00:15:42,440
Tangy.

211
00:15:42,750 --> 00:15:43,890
Is there anything to eat?

212
00:15:43,890 --> 00:15:45,100
Why did you come back so late?

213
00:15:45,100 --> 00:15:46,560
It's way past dinner time.

214
00:15:47,840 --> 00:15:49,610
I'll make you some instant noodles.

215
00:15:49,610 --> 00:15:51,470
Instant noodles aren't healthy.

216
00:15:52,670 --> 00:15:53,980
Should we order takeout?

217
00:15:53,980 --> 00:15:54,890
No.

218
00:15:55,370 --> 00:15:56,580
Other girlfriends

219
00:15:56,580 --> 00:15:57,200
make special handmade food

220
00:15:57,200 --> 00:15:58,800
for their boyfriends to eat.

221
00:15:59,580 --> 00:16:01,080
What do you mean?

222
00:16:01,270 --> 00:16:02,480
Don't even think about it.

223
00:16:02,480 --> 00:16:03,480
What do you mean by that?

224
00:16:03,480 --> 00:16:05,270
You don't know how to cook, do you?

225
00:16:05,270 --> 00:16:06,500
Of course I do.

226
00:16:09,630 --> 00:16:10,830
I'll make you a feast.

227
00:16:20,030 --> 00:16:21,630
Why are we having instant noodles?

228
00:16:21,630 --> 00:16:23,670
I might as well have ordered takeout.

229
00:16:23,670 --> 00:16:24,600
What's the rush?

230
00:16:24,600 --> 00:16:25,860
You'll see in a minute.

231
00:16:54,270 --> 00:16:55,270
It smells so good.

232
00:17:02,600 --> 00:17:03,840
Don't eat so fast.

233
00:17:05,290 --> 00:17:06,480
It's really delicious.

234
00:17:06,480 --> 00:17:07,030
Tangy.

235
00:17:07,180 --> 00:17:07,980
How did you come up with

236
00:17:07,980 --> 00:17:08,710
such a weird—

237
00:17:11,500 --> 00:17:13,089
I mean, such an amazing combination?

238
00:17:13,089 --> 00:17:14,089
It's incredible!

239
00:17:15,290 --> 00:17:16,200
When I was in college,

240
00:17:16,200 --> 00:17:17,530
I worked at a convenience store.

241
00:17:17,530 --> 00:17:19,660
That's when I came up with this recipe.

242
00:17:20,069 --> 00:17:22,030
I was so tired back then.

243
00:17:22,069 --> 00:17:24,220
And I still had to work night shifts
at the convenience store.

244
00:17:24,220 --> 00:17:26,329
Why did you have to work the night shift?

245
00:17:26,329 --> 00:17:28,190
It's so tough to stay up all night.

246
00:17:28,980 --> 00:17:30,590
The night shift paid more,

247
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:31,790
dummy.

248
00:17:34,240 --> 00:17:35,440
Do you know what the hardest part

249
00:17:35,440 --> 00:17:36,840
about the night shift is?

250
00:17:36,940 --> 00:17:39,400
It wasn't the sleepiness.
It was the hunger.

251
00:17:40,680 --> 00:17:41,570
Back then,

252
00:17:41,570 --> 00:17:43,530
all the restaurants
on the street were closed.

253
00:17:43,530 --> 00:17:45,680
There weren't food deliveries
at that hour too.

254
00:17:45,680 --> 00:17:47,140
So you just stayed hungry?

255
00:17:47,640 --> 00:17:49,370
That's when I came up with this.

256
00:17:49,590 --> 00:17:50,290
This convenience store sells lots of items

257
00:17:50,290 --> 00:17:52,640
that are close to their
expiration dates at a discount.

258
00:17:52,640 --> 00:17:53,840
They're super cheap.

259
00:17:54,070 --> 00:17:54,900
So I just put them

260
00:17:54,900 --> 00:17:56,500
all in here and turned it

261
00:17:56,500 --> 00:17:58,100
into a big mix of everything.

262
00:18:02,640 --> 00:18:04,410
When I took the first bite,

263
00:18:05,380 --> 00:18:07,180
I felt like I'd come back to life.

264
00:18:08,170 --> 00:18:09,830
Or maybe I was just too hungry,

265
00:18:10,240 --> 00:18:11,770
so everything tasted good.

266
00:18:12,240 --> 00:18:13,030
No.

267
00:18:13,090 --> 00:18:14,420
It's really delicious.

268
00:18:14,980 --> 00:18:15,590
I think

269
00:18:15,590 --> 00:18:17,320
it's better than a grand feast.

270
00:18:18,880 --> 00:18:20,440
Then you're lucky.

271
00:18:20,480 --> 00:18:22,270
It's my signature dish.

272
00:18:22,940 --> 00:18:25,090
So I'm the first one to try it?

273
00:18:27,520 --> 00:18:28,130
Then...

274
00:18:28,150 --> 00:18:29,630
I want to keep enjoying

275
00:18:29,790 --> 00:18:31,190
Tangy's exclusive dish.

276
00:18:33,180 --> 00:18:34,910
That depends on how you behave.

277
00:18:51,770 --> 00:18:53,170
That guy ran really fast.

278
00:18:53,440 --> 00:18:55,040
He suddenly knocked me over,

279
00:18:55,170 --> 00:18:56,570
and that's how I got hurt.

280
00:19:01,180 --> 00:19:02,980
Why aren't you saying anything?

281
00:19:19,250 --> 00:19:20,970
The doctor said I'm fine.

282
00:19:21,500 --> 00:19:24,220
It's just that the gift got broken

283
00:19:24,220 --> 00:19:26,080
just moments after it was bought.

284
00:19:33,500 --> 00:19:34,700
Can we still make it

285
00:19:34,700 --> 00:19:35,960
to the restaurant now?

286
00:19:37,660 --> 00:19:39,060
We're not going anymore.

287
00:19:39,500 --> 00:19:40,900
I'll take you home first.

288
00:19:46,610 --> 00:19:48,050
Hop on. I'll carry you.

289
00:19:49,600 --> 00:19:51,400
M-My hand is hurt,

290
00:19:51,400 --> 00:19:53,160
not my legs.

291
00:19:54,310 --> 00:19:55,370
I want to carry you.

292
00:20:00,420 --> 00:20:01,220
Fine.

293
00:20:01,250 --> 00:20:02,610
No one can tell

294
00:20:02,610 --> 00:20:03,870
where I'm hurt anyway.

295
00:20:17,900 --> 00:20:18,960
Does it still hurt?

296
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:22,720
I think this is the first time

297
00:20:22,720 --> 00:20:25,380
someone has carried me
like this since I grew up.

298
00:20:26,550 --> 00:20:27,830
Probably not.

299
00:20:30,310 --> 00:20:31,440
You don't remember?

300
00:20:32,420 --> 00:20:33,220
When?

301
00:20:34,350 --> 00:20:35,880
The last time you got drunk.

302
00:20:37,200 --> 00:20:38,700
You carried me home?

303
00:20:40,420 --> 00:20:41,750
I don't remember at all.

304
00:20:42,260 --> 00:20:43,280
Then am I

305
00:20:43,700 --> 00:20:45,000
heavier than last time?

306
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:46,600
Did I gain weight since then?

307
00:20:49,290 --> 00:20:50,090
Let me check.

308
00:20:51,660 --> 00:20:52,460
Am I heavy?

309
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:54,790
No.

310
00:20:56,700 --> 00:20:57,550
Really?

311
00:20:57,920 --> 00:20:58,350
No.

312
00:20:59,700 --> 00:21:00,810
What a shame.

313
00:21:01,290 --> 00:21:02,660
We didn't even have dinner.

314
00:21:02,660 --> 00:21:03,750
Jiameng said it's really hard

315
00:21:03,750 --> 00:21:05,280
to get a reservation there.

316
00:21:07,220 --> 00:21:08,010
It's okay.

317
00:21:08,250 --> 00:21:10,090
We can make a reservation another time.

318
00:21:10,090 --> 00:21:11,950
I'll cook for you when we get home.

319
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:12,850
You can cook?

320
00:21:15,850 --> 00:21:17,750
Forget it. Let's order takeout.

321
00:21:25,440 --> 00:21:26,010
Yun Lili,

322
00:21:28,460 --> 00:21:29,660
let's live together.

323
00:21:34,240 --> 00:21:34,740
The doctor said

324
00:21:34,740 --> 00:21:36,470
you need to keep your wound dry.

325
00:21:36,960 --> 00:21:39,360
I'm worried about you staying by yourself.

326
00:21:40,090 --> 00:21:40,590
I...

327
00:21:41,250 --> 00:21:41,790
I...

328
00:22:03,110 --> 00:22:04,910
You can sleep in my room tonight.

329
00:22:05,610 --> 00:22:07,720
Toiletries are in the bathroom.

330
00:22:09,330 --> 00:22:10,420
What about you?

331
00:22:12,510 --> 00:22:13,660
I need to go out again

332
00:22:14,040 --> 00:22:15,500
to take care of something.

333
00:22:18,210 --> 00:22:19,610
Go to sleep if you're tired.

334
00:22:19,610 --> 00:22:20,610
Don't wait for me.

335
00:22:23,770 --> 00:22:24,370
By the way,

336
00:22:24,790 --> 00:22:25,850
keep the wound dry.

337
00:22:26,080 --> 00:22:26,950
I know.

338
00:22:34,610 --> 00:22:35,590
It's so late.

339
00:22:35,750 --> 00:22:36,950
Wh-Where is he going?

340
00:22:51,790 --> 00:22:52,550
Shize.

341
00:22:54,270 --> 00:22:55,350
I found the guy.

342
00:22:55,510 --> 00:22:57,140
He's been caught by the police.

343
00:22:57,140 --> 00:22:58,870
Good. I'm glad they caught him.

344
00:25:31,470 --> 00:25:33,470
It's actually glued back together.

345
00:25:37,000 --> 00:25:38,250
Why aren't you wearing clothes?

346
00:25:38,250 --> 00:25:39,910
Put some clothes on right now.

347
00:25:42,920 --> 00:25:44,310
I am wearing clothes.

348
00:25:48,350 --> 00:25:50,350
I mean, proper clothes.

349
00:26:02,140 --> 00:26:03,340
Have you seen enough?

350
00:26:05,590 --> 00:26:07,200
Hurry up and change.

351
00:26:18,720 --> 00:26:19,920
Are you done?

352
00:26:24,940 --> 00:26:25,460
Done.

353
00:26:34,240 --> 00:26:35,220
Did you glue this

354
00:26:35,740 --> 00:26:37,470
aroma diffuser back together?

355
00:26:39,050 --> 00:26:40,310
I fixed it while you were asleep.

356
00:26:40,310 --> 00:26:42,970
Also, the thief
who knocked you down was caught.

357
00:26:58,220 --> 00:26:59,680
You can take a closer look.

358
00:26:59,760 --> 00:27:01,720
I... I'm afraid you'll...

359
00:27:06,440 --> 00:27:07,500
Help me dry my hair.

360
00:27:29,240 --> 00:27:29,720
Your...

361
00:27:31,290 --> 00:27:33,350
your shirt isn't buttoned properly.

362
00:28:37,700 --> 00:28:39,700
Are those all models?

363
00:28:42,140 --> 00:28:43,540
They're all functional.

364
00:28:43,740 --> 00:28:45,200
If you want to try them out,

365
00:28:45,240 --> 00:28:46,240
you can take them.

366
00:28:46,490 --> 00:28:48,290
They look very expensive.

367
00:28:48,550 --> 00:28:50,640
I can't afford
to replace one if I broke it.

368
00:28:50,640 --> 00:28:51,440
It's okay.

369
00:28:52,030 --> 00:28:53,230
What's mine is yours.

370
00:28:56,590 --> 00:28:57,160
Then,

371
00:28:57,160 --> 00:28:57,960
can I use them

372
00:28:57,960 --> 00:28:59,160
to record a video?

373
00:28:59,790 --> 00:29:01,530
I might need your help as well.

374
00:29:03,460 --> 00:29:04,290
Is that okay?

375
00:29:13,460 --> 00:29:14,790
Is there a reward for me?

376
00:29:15,940 --> 00:29:17,290
It's not like

377
00:29:17,290 --> 00:29:18,820
I need your help that badly.

378
00:29:20,960 --> 00:29:22,850
When my brother's in my videos,

379
00:29:22,850 --> 00:29:24,980
he doesn't ask for anything in return.

380
00:29:25,660 --> 00:29:27,050
Because he's your younger brother.

381
00:29:27,050 --> 00:29:28,250
He wouldn't dare ask.

382
00:29:28,250 --> 00:29:29,030
I don't boss my brother around

383
00:29:29,030 --> 00:29:30,480
that much, do I?

384
00:29:31,900 --> 00:29:32,420
I remember

385
00:29:32,420 --> 00:29:34,080
when you talk to your brother,

386
00:29:34,110 --> 00:29:35,870
you don't carefully ask him,

387
00:29:36,790 --> 00:29:37,650
"Is that okay?"

388
00:29:38,200 --> 00:29:40,400
That's because he's my little brother.

389
00:29:41,200 --> 00:29:42,640
But I'm your boyfriend.

390
00:29:44,680 --> 00:29:46,110
S-So?

391
00:29:48,400 --> 00:29:49,140
So you can

392
00:29:49,140 --> 00:29:50,540
be a little bossy with me.

393
00:29:52,790 --> 00:29:55,240
I... I'll try.

394
00:30:01,440 --> 00:30:02,010
Lili,

395
00:30:05,090 --> 00:30:06,330
nothing you say

396
00:30:07,750 --> 00:30:08,550
or do

397
00:30:09,400 --> 00:30:10,530
will change

398
00:30:11,750 --> 00:30:13,160
how much I like you.

399
00:30:16,070 --> 00:30:17,000
Same goes for me.

400
00:30:47,270 --> 00:30:47,930
Good night.

401
00:30:48,750 --> 00:30:49,410
Good night.

402
00:31:41,290 --> 00:31:42,200
Wh-What's up?

403
00:31:42,200 --> 00:31:42,880
Why did it take you so long

404
00:31:42,880 --> 00:31:44,010
to answer the phone?

405
00:31:45,090 --> 00:31:46,640
Where are you?

406
00:31:47,590 --> 00:31:48,570
In the restroom.

407
00:31:49,030 --> 00:31:50,210
The company restroom.

408
00:31:50,210 --> 00:31:51,530
W-What do you need?

409
00:31:52,900 --> 00:31:54,840
The Chinese New Year is coming.

410
00:31:54,870 --> 00:31:55,790
When are you coming home?

411
00:31:55,790 --> 00:31:56,220
Lili.

412
00:31:56,740 --> 00:31:57,870
Breakfast is ready.

413
00:31:57,960 --> 00:31:59,290
I-I'll be there soon.

414
00:32:00,510 --> 00:32:02,830
Why is there a man
in the women's restroom?

415
00:32:02,830 --> 00:32:04,110
And that voice sounds

416
00:32:04,140 --> 00:32:05,530
a bit familiar.

417
00:32:05,640 --> 00:32:06,530
You must've misheard.

418
00:32:06,530 --> 00:32:07,700
It's a female colleague.

419
00:32:07,700 --> 00:32:08,980
Her voice is hoarse.

420
00:32:09,740 --> 00:32:11,270
She must be very sick.

421
00:32:11,270 --> 00:32:12,700
Careful, don't catch whatever she's got.

422
00:32:12,700 --> 00:32:14,070
I-If you need anything, just say it.

423
00:32:14,070 --> 00:32:14,880
If there's nothing else, I'm hanging up.

424
00:32:14,880 --> 00:32:15,630
Wait, wait.

425
00:32:15,740 --> 00:32:17,680
Come home as soon as
your company breaks for the holiday.

426
00:32:17,680 --> 00:32:17,980
Got it.

427
00:32:17,980 --> 00:32:18,880
Bye-bye.

428
00:32:23,590 --> 00:32:25,190
So now I'm a female colleague

429
00:32:25,400 --> 00:32:26,530
with a hoarse voice?

430
00:32:26,830 --> 00:32:28,200
You heard that?

431
00:32:30,030 --> 00:32:30,960
Go wash up first.

432
00:32:31,000 --> 00:32:32,130
Breakfast is ready.

433
00:32:32,140 --> 00:32:32,940
I've washed up.

434
00:32:32,940 --> 00:32:34,470
I'll go have breakfast now.

435
00:32:52,740 --> 00:32:54,140
You're up so early.

436
00:32:57,000 --> 00:32:58,330
You are too, aren't you?

437
00:33:02,640 --> 00:33:05,400
This egg is perfectly fried.

438
00:33:07,570 --> 00:33:08,430
It's just okay.

439
00:33:15,530 --> 00:33:16,530
It smells so good.

440
00:33:20,850 --> 00:33:21,270
Here.

441
00:33:27,000 --> 00:33:28,500
Don't drink coffee on an empty stomach
early in the morning.

442
00:33:28,500 --> 00:33:29,960
It's bad for your stomach.

443
00:33:30,030 --> 00:33:30,830
Have mine.

444
00:33:33,640 --> 00:33:34,430
Okay.

445
00:33:34,730 --> 00:33:36,190
Just in case someone says,

446
00:33:36,330 --> 00:33:37,380
"How can anyone drink

447
00:33:37,380 --> 00:33:39,240
something that tastes this bad?"

448
00:33:39,680 --> 00:33:40,090
No.

449
00:33:40,750 --> 00:33:41,770
This time,

450
00:33:41,800 --> 00:33:44,500
I'll have the one with 70% sugar.

451
00:33:52,570 --> 00:33:53,830
Don't go to work today.

452
00:33:54,200 --> 00:33:56,600
I've already put in
a leave request for you.

453
00:33:57,790 --> 00:33:59,400
I'm fine now.

454
00:34:00,980 --> 00:34:02,580
Your hand hasn't healed yet.

455
00:34:04,090 --> 00:34:05,200
It's just a scratch.

456
00:34:05,200 --> 00:34:06,500
It won't affect my work.

457
00:34:06,500 --> 00:34:07,240
I'm fine.

458
00:34:12,630 --> 00:34:13,440
Lili,

459
00:34:14,880 --> 00:34:16,190
move in with me.

460
00:34:19,590 --> 00:34:21,120
I'm just worried about you.

461
00:34:22,040 --> 00:34:23,159
If you move in,

462
00:34:23,190 --> 00:34:24,650
we can go to work together.

463
00:34:24,670 --> 00:34:25,800
You'll be safer too.

464
00:34:30,150 --> 00:34:32,210
I don't want to see you get hurt again.

465
00:34:37,940 --> 00:34:38,650
Eat up.

466
00:34:42,389 --> 00:34:44,870
[Steal A Moment To Sip Wine Guesthouse]

467
00:34:45,630 --> 00:34:46,980
Come by again sometime.

468
00:34:47,940 --> 00:34:48,670
Take care.

469
00:34:52,800 --> 00:34:53,500
Zhengchu,

470
00:34:53,500 --> 00:34:55,070
I left your breakfast there.

471
00:34:55,070 --> 00:34:56,070
Okay, Congsheng.

472
00:34:57,780 --> 00:34:58,570
Morning.

473
00:34:59,780 --> 00:35:00,720
Tangy is here.

474
00:35:00,900 --> 00:35:02,230
Is this prepared for me?

475
00:35:05,360 --> 00:35:06,820
You're already eating it.

476
00:35:08,630 --> 00:35:09,980
Xia, have you eaten?

477
00:35:09,980 --> 00:35:10,570
This is for you.

478
00:35:10,570 --> 00:35:11,400
This is for Congsheng.

479
00:35:11,400 --> 00:35:12,330
This one is mine.

480
00:35:17,300 --> 00:35:18,590
I'd better eat outside

481
00:35:18,610 --> 00:35:20,810
before I end up throwing up on the floor.

482
00:35:38,650 --> 00:35:40,570
Where should I start?

483
00:35:45,080 --> 00:35:47,040
This puzzle is huge.

484
00:35:58,030 --> 00:35:59,010
Did you also sit here

485
00:35:59,010 --> 00:36:00,610
and work on it for a long time?

486
00:36:08,590 --> 00:36:09,380
Yun Li,

487
00:36:10,640 --> 00:36:12,440
you're already so close

488
00:36:12,470 --> 00:36:14,110
to your moon.

489
00:36:14,800 --> 00:36:16,670
It's almost within your reach.

490
00:36:22,190 --> 00:36:23,500
A piece is missing.

491
00:36:29,670 --> 00:36:31,030
Is this moving too fast?

492
00:36:33,670 --> 00:36:34,440
Why am I acting

493
00:36:34,440 --> 00:36:36,570
like I'm already the lady of the house?

494
00:36:37,650 --> 00:36:38,920
This is his puzzle.

495
00:36:38,920 --> 00:36:39,920
I should ask him.

496
00:36:46,290 --> 00:36:48,220
Let's start with the second floor.

497
00:37:35,780 --> 00:37:38,030
Why is there only water and alcohol?

498
00:37:40,440 --> 00:37:42,340
How does he get by like this?

499
00:37:57,880 --> 00:37:58,630
Lili,

500
00:37:59,090 --> 00:37:59,940
wake up.

501
00:38:00,190 --> 00:38:01,380
Rise and shine.

502
00:38:03,070 --> 00:38:05,000
You'll be late if you don't get up.

503
00:38:08,400 --> 00:38:09,360
I'm coming in.

504
00:38:16,570 --> 00:38:17,900
Things are moving fast.

505
00:38:58,380 --> 00:38:59,380
Hello, Tangy.

506
00:38:59,440 --> 00:39:00,510
Where are you?

507
00:39:00,820 --> 00:39:03,070
I'm outside.

508
00:39:03,350 --> 00:39:04,310
Outside?

509
00:39:05,070 --> 00:39:06,660
Where exactly?

510
00:39:07,010 --> 00:39:08,670
Did you sleep well last night?

511
00:39:09,520 --> 00:39:10,510
Was the blanket warm enough?

512
00:39:10,510 --> 00:39:12,010
You didn't catch a cold, did you?

513
00:39:12,010 --> 00:39:13,540
What are you talking about?

514
00:39:13,670 --> 00:39:14,730
Yun Li,

515
00:39:15,110 --> 00:39:17,230
I am Sherlock Tangy.

516
00:39:17,620 --> 00:39:19,420
You can't hide anything from me.

517
00:39:19,480 --> 00:39:21,550
You didn't come home last night.

518
00:39:22,210 --> 00:39:24,540
Something happened between you two, huh?

519
00:39:25,230 --> 00:39:26,360
Tell me everything.

520
00:39:26,530 --> 00:39:29,610
Confess and I'll go easy on you.
Resist, and you'll regret it.

521
00:39:29,610 --> 00:39:32,840
I'm at Fu Shize's place.

522
00:39:33,200 --> 00:39:35,130
You two are moving at rocket speed!

523
00:39:35,570 --> 00:39:36,480
Tell me.

524
00:39:36,480 --> 00:39:37,510
How did it go?

525
00:39:39,230 --> 00:39:40,880
Don't keep me in suspense.

526
00:39:41,010 --> 00:39:41,710
Details.

527
00:39:41,710 --> 00:39:42,820
I want details.

528
00:39:43,230 --> 00:39:43,880
Hold on!

529
00:39:43,880 --> 00:39:45,130
It's not what you think.

530
00:39:45,130 --> 00:39:47,480
S-Something just happened.

531
00:39:47,540 --> 00:39:49,310
Did you get him?

532
00:39:49,340 --> 00:39:51,440
I told you, it's not like that.

533
00:39:51,440 --> 00:39:52,440
It's just that...

534
00:39:53,130 --> 00:39:54,340
I was going to

535
00:39:54,340 --> 00:39:55,730
go out to dinner with him.

536
00:39:55,730 --> 00:39:57,440
Then I ran into a thief,

537
00:39:57,780 --> 00:39:59,230
and I hurt my hand.

538
00:40:00,730 --> 00:40:01,460
Are you okay?

539
00:40:01,480 --> 00:40:02,440
Is it serious?

540
00:40:02,530 --> 00:40:04,130
I'm fine. It's just a scrape.

541
00:40:05,780 --> 00:40:07,530
Then Fu Shize

542
00:40:07,530 --> 00:40:09,820
asked me to come live with him.

543
00:40:10,260 --> 00:40:11,570
You're moving in together?

544
00:40:11,570 --> 00:40:13,030
Who's moving in together?

545
00:40:13,110 --> 00:40:13,730
Lili.

546
00:40:13,730 --> 00:40:15,130
Let's talk when I see you later.

547
00:40:15,130 --> 00:40:15,920
Fu Zhengchu?

548
00:40:18,780 --> 00:40:20,510
If Fu Zhengchu knows,

549
00:40:21,680 --> 00:40:23,050
then Xia will know.

550
00:40:24,210 --> 00:40:25,130
If Xia knows,

551
00:40:25,130 --> 00:40:27,530
then Mr. Xu will definitely know.

552
00:40:27,530 --> 00:40:28,380
If Mr. Xu knows,

553
00:40:28,380 --> 00:40:29,380
then everyone at EAW

554
00:40:29,380 --> 00:40:29,880
will know.

555
00:40:29,880 --> 00:40:31,440
The whole world will know!

556
00:40:36,270 --> 00:40:38,400
Lili and Uncle are moving in together?

557
00:40:38,630 --> 00:40:40,710
What does that have to do with you?

558
00:40:42,960 --> 00:40:43,380
Tangy.

559
00:40:43,710 --> 00:40:44,980
Why don't you move in?

560
00:40:45,010 --> 00:40:46,200
Why would I move in?

561
00:40:46,480 --> 00:40:47,690
If Lili moves out,

562
00:40:47,690 --> 00:40:48,950
her room will be empty.

563
00:40:48,990 --> 00:40:49,870
It'd be a waste

564
00:40:49,900 --> 00:40:50,440
to leave it empty.

565
00:40:50,440 --> 00:40:52,030
Why don't you move in?

566
00:40:52,070 --> 00:40:53,980
It'll make your commute easier.

567
00:40:54,980 --> 00:40:57,170
So you're worried about the rent.

568
00:40:57,510 --> 00:40:58,420
Of course not.

569
00:40:58,820 --> 00:40:59,320
I was thinking

570
00:40:59,320 --> 00:41:00,480
it's hard for you

571
00:41:00,480 --> 00:41:01,340
to commute back and forth every day,

572
00:41:01,340 --> 00:41:02,600
whatever the weather.

573
00:41:06,090 --> 00:41:07,710
You know how to care for people?

574
00:41:07,710 --> 00:41:08,510
Of course.

575
00:41:09,840 --> 00:41:10,980
And if you move in,

576
00:41:10,980 --> 00:41:12,380
we can see each other more often.

577
00:41:12,380 --> 00:41:13,640
Wouldn't that be nice?

578
00:41:14,760 --> 00:41:16,160
Y-You call that nice?

579
00:41:16,630 --> 00:41:18,040
You just want me to be your

580
00:41:18,070 --> 00:41:19,320
24-hour nanny.

581
00:41:19,570 --> 00:41:20,840
In your dreams.

582
00:41:21,100 --> 00:41:22,390
Of course not.

583
00:41:23,530 --> 00:41:25,130
Give it some consideration.

584
00:41:25,340 --> 00:41:26,510
Stop talking nonsense.

585
00:41:26,510 --> 00:41:27,670
Hurry up and go to school.

586
00:41:27,670 --> 00:41:28,730
I have to go to work.

587
00:41:29,380 --> 00:41:30,240
Think about it.

588
00:41:31,440 --> 00:41:32,780
Get out of the way.

589
00:41:33,400 --> 00:41:34,010
Okay.

590
00:41:34,130 --> 00:41:35,260
I'm going to school.

591
00:41:35,610 --> 00:41:36,420
Bye-bye.

592
00:41:36,780 --> 00:41:37,680
Think about it.

593
00:42:04,420 --> 00:42:06,550
Is this calendar just for decoration?

594
00:42:07,940 --> 00:42:08,940
March 8th.

595
00:42:08,940 --> 00:42:10,320
It's already January.

596
00:42:24,880 --> 00:42:25,570
Shize,

597
00:42:25,570 --> 00:42:26,980
the work plan for February and March

598
00:42:26,980 --> 00:42:27,570
is out.

599
00:42:27,570 --> 00:42:29,230
Please review and confirm it.

600
00:42:34,500 --> 00:42:36,710
[March 8,
Light Chaser Global Launch Event]

601
00:42:39,480 --> 00:42:40,480
I have plans

602
00:42:41,280 --> 00:42:42,070
on March 8th.

603
00:42:42,910 --> 00:42:44,770
Do you have a date that day, Shize?

604
00:42:45,030 --> 00:42:45,730
I'll leave the press conference

605
00:42:45,730 --> 00:42:47,190
arrangements to you guys.

606
00:42:48,010 --> 00:42:48,780
Shize,

607
00:42:48,820 --> 00:42:50,710
you made a major contribution
to Light Chaser.

608
00:42:50,710 --> 00:42:52,190
If you don't come

609
00:42:52,210 --> 00:42:53,050
on a day worth celebrating...

610
00:42:53,050 --> 00:42:53,760
Chen.

611
00:42:55,210 --> 00:42:56,440
I'm not available that day.

612
00:42:56,440 --> 00:42:57,360
Shize, but...

613
00:42:57,380 --> 00:42:58,110
Chen.

614
00:42:59,920 --> 00:43:00,850
Get back to work.

615
00:43:00,920 --> 00:43:01,880
Okay, Mr. Xu.

616
00:43:11,530 --> 00:43:12,480
It's my fault.

617
00:43:12,880 --> 00:43:14,840
I should've checked more carefully.

618
00:43:14,840 --> 00:43:16,390
I know March 8th

619
00:43:16,420 --> 00:43:18,150
is the day you visit Jiang Yuan.

620
00:43:18,420 --> 00:43:20,420
Don't worry about the press conference.

621
00:43:20,420 --> 00:43:22,080
We can change the date, right?

622
00:43:22,780 --> 00:43:24,440
Just let me know once it's set.

623
00:43:25,510 --> 00:43:26,230
No need.

624
00:43:28,880 --> 00:43:31,130
Light Chaser is the result
of all our hard work.

625
00:43:31,130 --> 00:43:33,390
Everyone is looking forward to that day.

626
00:43:33,860 --> 00:43:34,700
Don't let my personal affairs

627
00:43:34,700 --> 00:43:36,300
become a burden to everyone.

628
00:43:37,060 --> 00:43:37,780
Let the press conference

629
00:43:37,780 --> 00:43:38,890
proceed as usual.

630
00:43:39,150 --> 00:43:40,070
I'll take care of

631
00:43:40,070 --> 00:43:41,930
my personal matters beforehand.

632
00:43:43,480 --> 00:43:44,280
Okay.

633
00:43:44,380 --> 00:43:45,170
Get back to work.
